The size of the tmpfs, which is how much of the memory of the node it may
hold.

It is set at every mount, and a resize grows the mounted tmpfs and records
the size it reached here. A volume of a shm pool points it at `{DEFAULT.size}`,
the size the volume was claimed with, so a resize of the volume records there.

It overrides a `size=` option of mnt_opt, which is then ignored.
